Application ID: scenario_058

## Business Domain

Enterprise Internal Developer Platform (IDP)

Large organizations centralize secret management through an Internal Developer Platform rather than allowing workloads to communicate directly with the enterprise secret backend. Applications request runtime secrets using logical aliases while the platform performs authentication, authorization, secret resolution, runtime materialization, and secure injection into the running workload.

Originally every secret alias uniquely identified a single secret. As the platform evolved to support multiple business domains, secret scopes were introduced so that the same logical alias could exist in multiple independent scopes. Runtime secret resolution must therefore uniquely identify a registered secret using both its alias and workload scope before materialization.

