Application ID: scenario_089

## Overview

An enterprise AI Operations platform enables autonomous agents to execute operational tools through multiple MCP-compatible Tool Providers. Backend services never perform provider selection directly; instead, they trust a `RuntimeCapability` produced by the capability pipeline and a provider selected by the runtime routing pipeline.

Execution is intentionally divided into two independent subsystems. The Security Platform team is responsible for policy approval and capability construction, while the Runtime Platform team is responsible for provider routing and execution. Both subsystems appear locally correct. The vulnerability only emerges when the approval pipeline and runtime pipeline converge.

## Architecture

```
UserRequest
      ↓
AgentGateway
      ↓
PolicyApprovalService
      ↓
CapabilityRepository
      ↓
CapabilityProjectionService
      ↓
RuntimeCapability
      ↓
ExecutionPlanner
      ↓
ExecutionScheduler
      ↓
ProviderResolver
      ↓
ExecutionDispatcher
      ↓
McpGateway
      ↓
AuditRecorder
