============================================================
APPLICATION DESCRIPTION
============================================================

Application ID: scenario_052

## Overview

An enterprise API gateway centralizes authorization for internal business services. Backend services never re-authenticate callers; they trust a `RuntimeAuthorizationContext` produced by the gateway.

Authorization is intentionally split into two independent pipelines. Branch A transforms the canonical `AuthorizationDecision` into a `CapabilityToken`. Branch B independently constructs a `RuntimePolicy` from the same decision. `GatewayMergeService` merges both into the `RuntimeAuthorizationContext` consumed by downstream services.

Both pipelines appear locally correct. The vulnerability only surfaces when they converge.

## Architecture

```
GatewayController
      ↓
PolicyEngine → AuthorizationDecision
      ↓                 ↓
CapabilityProjectionService   RuntimePolicyBuilder
      ↓                 ↓
CapabilityToken      RuntimePolicy
      ↓                 ↓
         GatewayMergeService
               ↓
     RuntimeAuthorizationContext
               ↓
         InvoiceService
               ↓
        InvoiceRepository → MongoDB
```


