Application ID: scenario_059

## Business Domain

Enterprise Design Collaboration Platform

A large enterprise operates an internal design collaboration platform used by engineering, product, design, and marketing teams.

Organizations own multiple projects, and every project contains numerous design files. Users are granted permissions to individual files rather than entire projects.

To improve performance, the platform separates authorization into multiple stages. Incoming requests are converted into a runtime permission context, authorization decisions are evaluated by a dedicated authorization engine, and previously computed authorization decisions are cached to reduce repeated evaluations.

Originally authorization existed only at the project level. After file-level authorization was introduced, every permission became uniquely identified by the combination of organization, project, file, and permission.

